---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {
  LEGAL_NAME, LEGAL_STATE, LEGAL_COUNTRY, POSTAL_ADDRESS,
  CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_PHONE, CONTACT_PHONE_E164,
} from '../data/legal';
const lastUpdated = '2026-09-21';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — JopChi"
  description="JopChi Privacy Policy: Firebase sign-in, cloud-saved stats, opt-in analytics that default to off, and what advertising collects."
>
  <article aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <!-- Draft notice -->
    <div class="draft-notice" role="alert" aria-live="polite">
      ⚠️ <strong>DRAFT — Pending Legal Review.</strong> This document has not yet
      been reviewed by legal counsel. Do not treat it as a final, binding privacy
      policy. Last updated: <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdated}</time>.
    </div>

    <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
    <h1 id="privacy-heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      JopChi ("we", "us", or "our") operates the JopChi iOS application and the
      website at <a href="https://jopchi.com">jopchi.com</a>. This
      Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, why we collect it, and how
      we protect it.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">
      Effective date: <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdated}</time><br />
      Contact: <a href="mailto:support@jopchi.com">support@jopchi.com</a><br />
      See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <nav aria-label="Privacy policy sections" class="toc">
      <h2 id="toc-heading">Contents</h2>
      <ol aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
        <li><a href="#section-identity">1. Who We Are</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-data-collected">2. Data We Collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-authentication">3. Authentication (Firebase)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-game-stats">4. Cloud-Stored Game Statistics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-analytics">5. Analytics (Opt-In)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-ads">6. Advertising</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-no-sale">7. Selling &amp; Sharing of Personal Data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-third-parties">8. Third-Party Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-data-retention">9. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-legal-basis">10. Legal Bases for Processing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-transfers">11. International Data Transfers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-children">12. Children's Privacy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-rights">13. Your Rights Under the GDPR</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-california">14. California Privacy Rights</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-changes">15. Changes to This Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-contact">16. Contact Us</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-identity">
      <h2 id="section-identity">1. Who We Are</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          JopChi is an independent iOS game published by <strong>{LEGAL_NAME}</strong>,
          an individual based in {LEGAL_STATE}, {LEGAL_COUNTRY}.
        </p>
        <p>
          {LEGAL_NAME} is the <strong>data controller</strong> for the personal
          data described in this policy, and can be reached at:
        </p>
        <address class="legal-address">
          {LEGAL_NAME}<br />
          {POSTAL_ADDRESS && <Fragment>{POSTAL_ADDRESS}<br /></Fragment>}
          {CONTACT_PHONE && CONTACT_PHONE_E164 && (
            <Fragment><a href={`tel:${CONTACT_PHONE_E164}`}>{CONTACT_PHONE}</a><br /></Fragment>
          )}
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
        </address>
        {(!POSTAL_ADDRESS || !CONTACT_PHONE) && (
          <p class="needs-input" role="note">
            <strong>[NEEDS INPUT]</strong> — a postal address and telephone
            number are still to be added, pending a decision on whether to use
            a business address and number rather than personal ones. Both are
            needed before release: GDPR Article 13 requires the controller's
            contact details, EU consumer rules expect a trader to be reachable
            other than by email, and Apple verifies and publishes a trader's
            name, address, phone and email on the EU App Store product page
            under Digital Services Act Articles 30-31.
          </p>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-data-collected">
      <h2 id="section-data-collected">2. Data We Collect</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>We collect only the data necessary to provide the game experience:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account identifiers</strong> — a unique user ID generated by Firebase Authentication, linked to your chosen sign-in method.</li>
          <li><strong>Display name / email</strong> — provided by your Apple, Google, or Facebook account at sign-in, used solely to personalise your experience.</li>
          <li><strong>Game statistics</strong> — puzzle attempt counts, scores, streaks, and timestamps, stored in Firebase Firestore.</li>
          <li><strong>Device information</strong> — iOS version and device model, collected by Firebase automatically for crash reporting.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics events</strong> — only if you opt in. See section 5.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising identifiers</strong> — only where ads are served and you have permitted tracking. See section 6.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect precise location, contacts, photos, health data, or any other sensitive category.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-authentication">
      <h2 id="section-authentication">3. Authentication (Firebase)</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          JopChi uses <strong>Firebase Authentication</strong> (provided by Google LLC)
          to manage sign-in. You can play as a guest without an account. If you
          do sign in, we support three providers:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Sign in with Apple</strong> — Apple may provide a
            private relay email address. We store only what Apple sends us.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> — Google provides your name and
            email address. We store only what Google sends us.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sign in with Facebook</strong> — Facebook provides your name and
            email address. We store only what Facebook sends us.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Firebase Authentication data is processed under Google's <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Firebase Privacy and Security documentation</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-game-stats">
      <h2 id="section-game-stats">4. Cloud-Stored Game Statistics</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          Your puzzle results, streaks, and daily scores are stored in <strong>Firebase Firestore</strong>, allowing you to resume your
          progress across devices. This data is associated with your Firebase
          user ID and is not publicly visible to other players unless you
          explicitly share a result.
        </p>
        <p>
          Firebase Firestore is operated by Google LLC and governed by the <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-addendum" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Cloud Data Processing Addendum</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-analytics">
      <h2 id="section-analytics">5. Analytics (Opt-In)</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          JopChi uses <strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> to understand how the
          game is played. It is <strong>off by default</strong>: a fresh install
          collects nothing until you agree, and you can change your mind at any
          time from Settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you have not opted in, collection is disabled in two places. The
          app issues no analytics calls, and the Firebase SDK's own automatic
          events — session starts, screen views, app updates — are switched off
          as well. Opting out means <strong>no analytics events at all</strong>,
          not merely fewer.
        </p>
        <p>When analytics is enabled, we deliberately never send:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Authentication tokens</li>
          <li>Email addresses, display names, or avatar URLs</li>
          <li>Any free text you type, including your guesses</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Event parameters and user properties are a fixed, limited list. The
          only identifier attached is your pseudonymous Firebase user ID.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-ads">
      <h2 id="section-ads">6. Advertising</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          JopChi is free to play and supported by advertising. Ads are served by
          third-party advertising networks, which act as independent controllers
          of the data they collect:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> — <a href="https://business.safety.google/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>AppLovin MAX</strong> — <a href="https://www.applovin.com/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AppLovin Privacy Policy</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These networks may collect device and usage signals in order to
          deliver and measure ads. On iOS, personalised advertising can involve
          the <strong>Identifier for Advertisers (IDFA)</strong>, and Apple's <strong>App Tracking Transparency</strong> framework governs access to
          it: we can only use that identifier if you grant permission when
          asked. Declining is a fully supported choice that leaves the game
          identical, and you can change it at any time in <em>iOS Settings &rsaquo; Privacy &amp; Security &rsaquo; Tracking</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where required, an ad network's own consent flow will ask about
          personalised advertising before any personalised ad is shown.
          Declining means you still see ads, but non-personalised ones.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Removing ads.</strong> A one-time in-app purchase permanently
          removes advertising from the app. See our <a href="/terms#section-purchases">Terms of Service</a> for how that purchase works.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-no-sale">
      <h2 id="section-no-sale">7. Selling &amp; Sharing of Personal Data</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data for money, and we do
          not share it with data brokers or analytics resellers.
        </p>
        <p>
          You should know that under some privacy laws — notably the California
          Consumer Privacy Act as amended — the terms &ldquo;sell&rdquo; and
          &ldquo;share&rdquo; are defined broadly, and serving <strong>personalised
          advertising</strong> can fall within them even when no money changes
          hands. If you would rather that did not happen, you have two
          independent ways to prevent it: decline tracking when Apple asks, or
          remove advertising entirely with the in-app purchase. Section 14
          describes your California rights in more detail.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-third-parties">
      <h2 id="section-third-parties">8. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>We use the following third-party services, each with their own privacy policies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Authentication, Firestore, Crashlytics, Analytics) — <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> — <a href="https://business.safety.google/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>AppLovin MAX</strong> — <a href="https://www.applovin.com/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AppLovin Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Apple Sign In</strong> — <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Apple Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Google Sign In</strong> — <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Facebook Login</strong> — <a href="https://www.facebook.com/policy.php" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Facebook Data Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Apple App Store</strong> — processes all in-app purchases. We never receive or store your payment details.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Beyond those listed above, we integrate no other analytics, tracking, or advertising libraries.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-data-retention">
      <h2 id="section-data-retention">9. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          We retain your account and game statistics for as long as your account
          is active. You may request deletion of your account and associated data
          at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@jopchi.com">support@jopchi.com</a>.
          We will process deletion requests within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Crash logs collected by Firebase Crashlytics are automatically purged
          after 90 days per Google's standard retention schedule.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data held by the advertising networks in section 6 is retained under
          their own policies and schedules, not ours. Deleting your JopChi
          account does not erase records those networks hold independently;
          their privacy policies explain how to make requests directly to them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-legal-basis">
      <h2 id="section-legal-basis">10. Legal Bases for Processing</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          We are established outside the EU, but JopChi is offered to players
          in the EU, so the GDPR applies to this processing under Article 3(2).
          We rely on the following legal bases:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Performance of a contract</strong> (Article 6(1)(b)) — creating your account, saving your streak and statistics, and delivering a purchase you have made.</li>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> (Article 6(1)(a)) — analytics, and personalised advertising. Both are off until you agree, and both are withdrawable at any time without losing access to the game.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)) — crash reporting and keeping the service secure and working. Our interest is in a game that does not crash; the data is limited to device model, OS version, and diagnostics.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Where we rely on consent, withdrawing it is as easy as giving it, and
          does not affect processing that already took place while consent was
          in force.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-transfers">
      <h2 id="section-transfers">11. International Data Transfers</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          We operate from the United States, and our service providers —
          Google (Firebase), Apple, Meta, and the advertising networks in
          section 6 — process data on infrastructure that may sit outside the
          European Economic Area. If you are in the EU or EEA, your data will
          therefore be transferred out of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those transfers rely on the safeguards each provider offers under
          Chapter V of the GDPR, principally the European Commission's <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses</strong> and, where applicable,
          the provider's certification under the EU&ndash;US Data Privacy
          Framework. Google's terms for Firebase are set out in the <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-addendum" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Cloud Data Processing Addendum</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-children">
      <h2 id="section-children">12. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          JopChi is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or the
          equivalent minimum digital age of consent in your jurisdiction). We
          do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you
          believe a child has provided us with personal information, please
          contact <a href="mailto:support@jopchi.com">support@jopchi.com</a> and we will delete it promptly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-rights">
      <h2 id="section-rights">13. Your Rights Under the GDPR</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you, and receive a copy</li>
          <li><strong>Rectify</strong> data that is inaccurate or incomplete</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — have your account and its data deleted</li>
          <li><strong>Restrict</strong> or <strong>object to</strong> certain processing</li>
          <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your data in a machine-readable form</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, for analytics or personalised ads</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We respond
          within one month, as the GDPR requires, and we do not charge for it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two of them you can exercise yourself, immediately, without contacting
          us at all: analytics consent is reversible from Settings, and tracking
          permission is reversible in iOS Settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you believe we have handled your data improperly you may lodge a
          complaint with the data protection authority in your own country. We
          are not established in the EU, so there is no single lead supervisory
          authority for us; your national authority is the right place to go,
          and EU residents can find theirs through the <a href="https://www.edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">European Data Protection Board</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="needs-input" role="note">
          <strong>[NEEDS INPUT]</strong> — GDPR Article 27 requires a
          controller outside the EU that offers services to EU residents to
          designate a <strong>representative in the Union</strong>, unless the
          processing is occasional, low-risk and involves no large-scale
          special-category data. Whether the exemption covers a daily game with
          advertising is a judgement call for counsel. If a representative is
          appointed, their name and address must be published here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-california">
      <h2 id="section-california">14. California Privacy Rights</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          Where the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended applies to us,
          California residents have the right to know what personal information is
          collected, to request its deletion or correction, to opt out of its
          sale or sharing for cross-context behavioural advertising, and not to
          be discriminated against for exercising any of those rights.
        </p>
        <p>
          To opt out of personalised advertising, decline tracking when Apple
          asks, or turn it off later in <em>iOS Settings &rsaquo; Privacy &amp; Security &rsaquo; Tracking</em>.
          Removing ads with the in-app purchase also ends it. The game remains
          fully playable either way, with identical stats, streaks, and
          features — we do not offer a worse experience to anyone who opts out.
        </p>
        <p>
          For any other request, email <a href="mailto:support@jopchi.com">support@jopchi.com</a>.
          We may need to verify that the request genuinely comes from you, and
          you may use an authorised agent.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-changes">
      <h2 id="section-changes">15. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will
          revise the "effective date" at the top of this page. Continued use of
          JopChi after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="section-contact">
      <h2 id="section-contact">16. Contact Us</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          For any privacy-related questions or requests: <a href="mailto:support@jopchi.com">support@jopchi.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article { max-width: 52rem; }

  .page-intro {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .toc {
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .toc h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .toc ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.2rem 1rem;
  }

  .toc a {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  } 

  section { margin-top: 2.5rem; } 
  section h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }

  .legal-address {
    font-style: normal;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* An item still awaiting a decision before publication — deliberately loud */
  .needs-input {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid #fbbf24;
    background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #fde68a;
  }
</style>
